  "question": "Let $C_1$ and $C_2$ be the circles given by the equations $x^2+y^2-4x-5=0$ and $x^2+y^2+8y+7=0$. Then the circle having the common chord of $C_1$ and $C_2$ as its diameter has",
  "options": {
    "A": "centre at $(-1,-1)$ and radius 2",
    "B": "centre at $(1,-2)$ and radius $2\\sqrt3$",
    "C": "centre at $(1,-2)$ and radius 2",
    "D": "centre at $(3,-3)$ and radius 2"
  },
  "answer": "C",
